Steam Enhanced, client/home/stage/tray.js: a collection card on the Home board is never narrower than
~160 px.

Why. fitColl() gives the Collections panel 2 cards across for every 4 of the board's 12 columns it
spans, counted from its share of the board. Under 1300 px of board the board has 8 columns and a
half-width panel counts as 6 of 12 (round(1.5) = 2): 4 cards across in ~430-600 px. On a 1920×1080
window the cards were ~135 px wide and a name had 68 px ("// MICR…", "Избран…"); at 1366×768 and at
125-150 % scale 95 px, names were 3 letters and "43 игры" wrapped onto a second line.

What. The columns from the panel's span are capped by what the grid's width holds at 160 px a card
(GAP between): (W + GAP) / (160 + GAP), at least 1. Wide boards keep their columns (a card there is
200 px and more); fewer columns show fewer cards in the same 3 rows, the rest behind "+N" as before.

--- a/client/home/stage/tray.js
+++ b/client/home/stage/tray.js
@@ -316,7 +316,10 @@
     // 12 columns the panel spans (2, 4, 6: 6, 12 or 18 cards), the rows sharing the cell's
     // height; one card across when the cell is very narrow
     const ROWS = 3;
-    const cols = W > 0 && W < 300 ? 1 : (tilesAcross(entry.el) / 3) * 2;
+    // A card never narrower than CARD_MIN (its name and the fan of covers): fewer across then
+    const CARD_MIN = 160;
+    const room = W > 0 ? Math.max(1, Math.floor((W + GAP) / (CARD_MIN + GAP))) : Infinity;
+    const cols = W > 0 && W < 300 ? 1 : Math.min(room, (tilesAcross(entry.el) / 3) * 2);
     const fit = cols * ROWS;
     const cardH = H > 0 ? Math.floor(((H - GAP * (ROWS - 1)) / ROWS) * 100) / 100 : 104;
 
